<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Miner dies in Winkelhaak blasting accident.</title>
<headline>Miner dies in Winkelhaak blasting accident.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>One miner was killed and two others injured in an underground blasting accident at South African mining house Gencor Ltd's Winkelhaak mine on Wednesday night, the company said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;It was a blasting accident which happened in an old area of the mine, it will have no impact on production,&quot; Gengold company secretary Trevor Savage told Reuters.</p>
<p>The two injured miners were in a satisfactory condition in hospital.</p>
<p>Winkelhaak, a division of Evander Gold Mines Ltd produced 1,761 kg of gold in the three months to end-December.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27-11 482 1003</p>
</text>
